==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|compressen}}, from {{der|en|fro|compresser}}, from {{der|en|la-lat|compressare||to press hard/together}}, from {{der|en|la|compressus}}, the past participle of {{m|la|comprimō||to compress}}, itself from {{m|la|com-||together}} + {{m|la|premō||press}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/kəmˈpɹɛs/}}, {{enPR|kəmprĕs'}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-compress-verb.ogg|a=US|pos=verb}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛs|s=2}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make smaller; to [[press]] or [[squeeze]] together, or to make something occupy a smaller space or volume.
#: {{syn|en|compact|condense|pack|press|squash|squeeze|Thesaurus:compress}}
#: {{ant|en|expand}}
#: {{ux|en|The force required to '''compress''' a spring varies linearly with the displacement.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=June 17 1825|author=w:Daniel Webster|journal=Speech on the laying of the Corner Stone of the Bunker Hill Monument|passage=events of centuries {{...}} '''compressed''' within the compass of a single life}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1810|translator=William Melmoth|title=Letters of Pliny
|passage=The same strength of expression, though more '''compressed''', runs through his historical harangues.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be pressed together or [[folded]] by [[compression]] into a more economic, easier format.
#: {{syn|en|contract}}
#: {{ant|en|decontract}}
#: {{ux|en|Our new model '''compresses''' easily, ideal for storage and travel}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[condense]] into a more economic, easier format.
#: {{ux|en|This chart '''compresses''' the entire audit report into a few lines on a single diagram.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[abridge]].
#: {{syn|en|abridge|condense|shorten|truncate|Thesaurus:shorten}}
#: {{ant|en|expand|lengthen}}
#: {{ux|en|If you try to '''compress''' the entire book into a three-sentence summary, you will lose a lot of information.}}
# {{lb|en|computing|transitive}} To make digital information smaller by [[encode|encoding]] it using fewer [[bit]]s.
#: {{syn|en|zip}}
#: {{ant|en|uncompress|decompress|unzip}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|author=Vince Buffalo|title=Bioinformatics Data Skills{{...|: Reproducible and Robust Research with Open Source Tools}}|publisher=O'Reilly|isbn=9781449367503|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=FRERCgAAQBAJ&pg=PT135&dq=%22compress%22+files&hl=&cd=3&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22compress%22%20files&f=false|text=The command-line tool <code>gzip</code> allows you to '''compress''' files in a few different ways. First, <code>gzip</code> can '''compress''' results from standard input.}}
# {{lb|en|physics|transitive}} To make a [[pulse]] or [[particle]] [[bunch]] shorter by applying [[dispersion]] to it.
#: {{ant|en|stretch}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2019|author=B. Webb ''et al.''|title=Simulation of grating compressor misalignment tolerances and mitigation strategies for chirped-pulse–amplification systems of varying bandwidths and beam sizes|journal=Applied Optics|url=|volume=58|issue=2|page=234-243|text=Diffraction gratings are by far the most common elements used to stretch and '''compress''' pulses because of their substantial angular dispersion, {{...}}|t=}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To embrace sexually.
#* {{RQ:Pope Works|volume=I|title=Dryope|page=295|passage=This nymph '''compreſs'd''' by him vvho rules the day, / VVhom ''Delphi'' and the ''Delian'' iſle obey, / ''Andræmon'' lov'd; and, bleſs'd in all thoſe charms / That pleas'd a God, ſucceeded to her arms.}}

