===Etymology 2===
From {{bor|en|frm|compresse}}, from {{m|frm|compresse|t=to compress}}, from {{der|en|la-lat|compressare||to press hard/together}}, from {{der|en|la|compressus}}, the past participle of {{m|la|comprimō||to compress}}, itself from {{m|la|com-||together}} + {{m|la|premō||press}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɒmpɹɛs/|a=RP}}
* {{enPR|kŏm'prĕs|a=US}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈkɑmpɹɛs/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-compress-noun.ogg|a=US|pos=noun}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|folded_cloth}} {{lb|en|medicine}} A multiply folded piece of [[cloth]], a [[pouch]] of [[ice]], etc., used to apply to a patient's skin, cover the dressing of wounds, and placed with the aid of a [[bandage]] to apply [[pressure]] on an injury.
#: {{ux|en|He held a cold '''compress''' over the sprain.}}
# A machine for [[compressing]].

